-- title:
--   Toffoli gate from single-qubit and two-qubit gates
-- statement:
--   On three qubits, the Toffoli (CCNOT) gate $|a,b,c\rangle\mapsto|a,b,c\oplus ab\rangle$ lies in the subgroup of $U(8)$ generated by single-qubit gates and CNOTs:
--   $$\mathrm{Toffoli}\in\big\langle\,\mathcal S_3\cup\mathcal G_3(\mathrm{CNOT})\,\big\rangle .$$
--
--   That is, the three-qubit Toffoli gate is an exact finite product of single- and two-qubit gates, as used in its experimental realisation on three superconducting transmon qubits.
-- source:
--   Wikipedia, "Superconducting quantum computing" (PDF snapshot supplied by the mission author, retrieved 2026-10-13), https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superconducting_quantum_computing; section 'Quantum gates', figure caption: 'A three qubit Toffoli gate (CCNOT) is implemented using a combination of single and two-qubit gates' (article ref. [23]); Nielsen & Chuang Fig. 4.9

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SuperconductingQC_Gates

open scoped Matrix Kronecker

namespace SuperconductingQC

theorem toffoli_mem_closure_singleQubit_CNOT :
    ∃ W ∈ Subgroup.closure (singleQubitGates 3 ∪ twoQubitGateInstances 3 CNOT),
      (W : Matrix (Fin 3 → Fin 2) (Fin 3 → Fin 2) ℂ) = toffoli := by
  sorry

end SuperconductingQC
